3LmQw8eR\", 60);\n    65\t  w.member(\"M1003\", \"박서연\", \" IOS:Zx81kQpLm0Ty \", 30);\n    66\t  w.member(\"M1004\", \"최민준\", \"and:Pq19sXkLm2Vb\", 10);\n    67\t  w.member(\"M1005\", \"정지우\", \"ios:Nn41tRe7Ku3Q\", 1440);\n    68\t\n    69\t  const phone = w.autopay(\"M1001\", \"한빛모바일 통신요금\", 55000, 12, \"08:00\");\n    70\t  w.autopay(\"M1002\", \"든든손해보험\", 89000, 12, \"10:20\");\n    71\t  w.autopay(\"M1003\", \"스트림플러스 구독\", 13900, 12, \"13:47\");\n    72\t  w.autopay(\"M1004\", \"푸른마을 관리비\", 187420, 12, \"18:33\");\n    73\t  w.autopay(\"M1005\", \"새싹수학학원\", 320000, 12, \"09:00\");\n    74\t\n    75\t  const plan = w.plan(\"2026-10-12\");\n    76\t  eq([plan.planned, plan.scheduled], [5, 5], \"reminders planned for the 12th\");\n    77\t\n    78\t  // 08:00 출금이 잔액 부족으로 실패 → 2시간 뒤 재출금, 그 30분 전에 안내\n    79\t  w.clock(\"2026-10-12T08:00:37\");\n    80\t  w.fail(phone, \"2026-10-12T08:00:37\");\n    81\t  w.clock(\"2026-10-12T23:59:00\");\n    82\t\n    83\t  const r = w.report(\"2026-10-12\");\n    84\t  eq(r.lines.filter((l) => l.status !== \"발송\").map((l) => `${l.memberId} ${l.kind}`), [], \"reminders not delivered\");\n    85\t  eq([r.planned, r.delivered, r.missing], [6, 6, 0], `report counts (${r.text})`);\n    86\t\n    87\t  // 고객이 설정한 시점보다 늦게 도착하면 안 된다\n    88\t  const latest: [string, string[], string][] = [\n    89\t    [\"M1001\", [\"2026-10-12T07:30:00\", \"2026-10-12T09:30:37\"], \"한빛모바일\"],\n    90\t    [\"M1002\", [\"2026-10-12T09:20:00\"], \"든든손해보험\"],\n    91\t    [\"M1003\", [\"2026-10-12T13:17:00\"], \"스트림플러스\"],\n    92\t    [\"M1004\", [\"2026-10-12T18:23:00\"], \"푸른마을\"],\n    93\t    [\"M1005\", [\"2026-10-11T09:00:00\"], \"새싹수학학원\"],\n    94\t  ];\n    95\t  for (const [id, deadlines, merchant] of latest) {\n    96\t    const inbox = w.inbox(id);\n    97\t    eq(inbox.length, deadlines.length, `pushes received by ${id}`);\n    98\t    inbox.forEach((n, i) => {\n    99\t      assert(n.at <= deadlines[i], `${id} push #${i + 1} arrived at ${n.at}, later than ${deadlines[i]}`);\n   100\t      assert(n.message.includes(merchant), `${id} push mentions ${merchant}`);\n   101\t    });\n   102\t  }\n   103\t});\n   104\t\n   105\ttest(\"customers who turned pushes off are skipped and counted\", () => {\n   106\t  const w = world();\n   107\t  w.member(\"M2001\", \"한지민\", \"ios:Aa11bB22cC33\", 30);\n   108\t  w.member(\"M2002\", \"오세훈\", \"and:Dd44eE55fF66\", 30, false);\n   109\t  w.autopay(\"M2001\", \"든든손해보험\", 42000, 3, \"09:00\");\n   110\t  w.autopay(\"M2002\", \"든든손해보험\", 42000, 3, \"09:00\");\n   111\t  const plan = w.plan(\"2026-11-03\");\n   112\t  eq([plan.planned, plan.skippedOptOut], [1, 1], \"planned / opted out\");\n   113\t  w.clock(\"2026-11-03T12:00:00\");\n   114\t  eq(w.inbox(\"M2001\").length, 1, \"opted-in customer\");\n   115\t  eq(w.inbox(\"M2002\"), [], \"opted-out customer\");\n   116\t});\n   117\t\n   118\ttest(\"planning the same day twice does not double-book, and cancelled contracts stay quiet\", () => {\n   119\t  const w = world();\n   120\t  w.member(\"M3001\", \"서지호\", \"ios:Gg77hH88iI99\", 60);\n   121\t  w.member(\"M3002\", \"윤시우\", \"and:Jj00kK11lL22\", 30);\n   122\t  w.autopay(\"M3001\", \"한빛모바일 통신요금\", 61000, 20, \"11:00\");\n   123\t  const gym = w.autopay(\"M3002\", \"바른필라테스\", 99000, 20, \"07:30\");\n   124\t  eq(w.plan(\"2026-10-20\").scheduled, 2, \"first planning\");\n   125\t  const again = w.plan(\"2026-10-20\");\n   126\t  eq([again.scheduled, again.alreadyScheduled], [0, 2], \"second planning\");\n   127\t  w.cancel(gym);\n   128\t  w.clock(\"2026-10-20T23:00:00\");\n   129\t  eq(w.inbox(\"M3001\").length, 1, \"one reminder, not two\");\n   130\t  eq(w.inbox(\"M3002\"), [], \"cancelled contract\");\n   131\t});\n   132\t\n   133\trun();\n==== tests/time.test.ts\n     1\timport { QuietHours } from \"../src/scheduling/quietHours\";\n     2\timport { SendTimePolicy } from \"../src/scheduling/sendTime\";\n     3\timport { addMinutes, at, compare, isLocalDateTime, previousDate } from \"../src/time/localTime\";\n     4\timport { eq, run, test } from \"./harness\";\n     5\t\n     6\ttest(\"minute arithmetic crosses days, months and leap days\", () => {\n     7\t  eq(addMinutes(\"2026-10-12T00:10:00\", -30), \"2026-10-11T23:40:00\", \"back over midnight\");\n     8\t  eq(addMinutes(\"2026-11-01T09:00:00\", -1440), \"2026-10-31T09:00:00\", \"back over month end\");\n     9\t  eq(addMinutes(\"2028-02-28T23:30:00\", 60), \"2028-02-29T00:30:00\", \"leap day\");\n    10\t  eq(previousDate(\"2026-01-01\"), \"2025-12-31\", \"previous date over year end\");\n    11\t});\n    12\t\n    13\ttest(\"local time validation rejects impossible dates\", () => {\n    14\t  eq(isLocalDateTime(\"2026-02-30T10:00:00\"), false, \"Feb 30\");\n    15\t  eq(isLocalDateTime(\"2026-10-12T24:00:00\"), false, \"hour 24\");\n    16\t  eq(isLocalDateTime(\"2026-10-12 10:00:00\"), false, \"space separator\");\n    17\t  eq(isLocalDateTime(\"2026-10-12T10:00:59\"), true, \"valid\");\n    18\t  eq(compare(at(\"2026-10-12\", \"10:20\"), \"2026-10-12T10:19:59\") > 0, true, \"ordering\");\n    19\t});\n    20\t\n    21\ttest(\"quiet hours pull a reminder back to the previous evening\", () => {\n    22\t  const policy = new SendTimePolicy(new QuietHours(\"22:00\", \"07:00\", \"21:00\"));\n    23\t  eq(policy.sendAt(\"2026-10-12T07:00:00\", 60), \"2026-10-11T21:00:00\", \"06:00 → evening before\");\n    24\t  eq(policy.sendAt(\"2026-10-12T23:30:00\", 30), \"2026-10-12T21:00:00\", \"23:00 → same evening\");\n    25\t  eq(policy.sendAt(\"2026-10-12T09:00:00\", 30), \"2026-10-12T08:30:00\", \"daytime unchanged\");\n    26\t  eq(policy.sendAt(\"2026-10-12T07:10:00\", 10), \"2026-10-12T07:00:00\", \"quiet end is exclusive\");\n    27\t});\n    28\t\n    29\trun();\n==== tests/harness.ts\n     1\ttype Fn = () => void;\n     2\tconst registered: [string, Fn][] = [];\n     3\tconst cleanups: (() => void)[] = [];\n     4\t\n     5\texport function test(name: string, fn: Fn): void {\n     6\t  registered.push([name, fn]);\n     7\t}\n     8\t\n     9\texport function onCleanup(fn: () => void): void {\n    10\t  cleanups.push(fn);\n    11\t}\n    12\t\n    13\texport function eq(actual: unknown, expected: unknown, label: string): void {\n    14\t  const a = JSON.stringify(actual);\n    15\t  const e = JSON.stringify(expected);\n    16\t  if (a !== e) throw new Error(`${label}: expected ${e}, got ${a}`);\n    17\t}\n    18\t\n    19\texport function assert(cond: boolean, label: string): void {\n    20\t  if (!cond) throw new Error(label);\n    21\t}\n    22\t\n    23\texport function run(): void {\n    24\t  let failed = 0;\n    25\t  for (const [name, fn] of registered) {\n    26\t    try {\n    27\t      fn();\n    28\t      console.log(`ok   - ${name}`);\n    29\t    } catch (e) {\n    30\t      failed++;\n    31\t      console.log(`FAIL - ${name}: ${e instanceof Error ? e.message : String(e)}`);\n    32\t    }\n    33\t  }\n    34\t  for (const c of cleanups) {\n    35\t    try {\n    36\t      c();\n    37\t    } catch {\n    38\t      /* ignore */\n    39\t    }\n    40\t  }\n    41\t  console.log(failed === 0 ? \"all passed\" : `${failed} failed`);\n    42\t  process.exitCode = failed === 0 ? 0 : 1;\n    43\t}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BUiL3334DjK7vXaFYQCTi4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
